WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:04.722
Need a breather? Pause the ride, or end it.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.760
While the ride runs, the app bar shows the clock, Pause and End.

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.371
Press Pause, and a Paused badge appears.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.830
The clock holds at seven oh seven, and the bike stays at its level.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.230
Press Resume, and the ride picks up from the same second.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.138
Press End, and Wattzup asks first: End this ride?

00:00:41.338 --> 00:00:45.066
Keep riding has the focus, so a stray tap changes nothing.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:53.450
End ride reads Ending while the server stops the workout.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.561
The ride is over, but your power trace and totals stay on the dashboard until you

00:01:02.561 --> 00:01:03.818
start a new ride.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:10.963
On a phone, the same dialog, the same choice.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.609
What the tests prove: resume continues from the same point.

00:01:19.809 --> 00:01:23.731
And a paused ride is never shut off while the bike stays connected.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.564
That is journey seven. Wattzup turns an Echelon bike or treadmill into a live

00:01:32.564 --> 00:01:33.872
training display.
